    <title>Typical Superpositions are Magical</title>
    <summary>  The non-stabilizerness, or "magic", of a quantum state is a common metric
for the hardness of simulation on a classical computer. We show that typical
superpositions of stabilizer states are magical.
</summary>
    <author><name>Joshuah T. Heath</name></author>
